      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7bh",
          "text": "If you need assistance determining the cause of your truck accident, an attorney can revisit the scene of the crash, hire experts and take other steps to identify the defendant(s) in your case.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7bk",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7bj",
          "text": "Who Is Liable in a Colorado Truck Accident?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7bm",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7bl",
          "text": "Liability, or legal and financial responsibility, for a truck accident, will fall to the person or party at fault for causing the crash in Colorado. This is because the state uses a tort-based insurance law. Before you can file a claim, you must identify the person or party who caused your crash. What is unique about a truck accident, however, is that trucking companies are vicariously liable for their truck drivers and employees under federal law. This means that if a truck driver caused your crash, you can file a claim against the trucking company, in most cases.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7bo",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7bn",
          "text": "What Damages Are Available in a Colorado Truck Accident Case?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b7bq",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s7bp",
          "text": "A successful truck accident claim in Colorado could repay you for many costs and losses associated with your crash. The results that you achieve with assistance from an attorney can help you and your family move forward with greater financial peace of mind. You may be entitled to recover compensation for many past and future losses, including:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
